<title>NETHERLANDS: German natural gas imports dip 3.7 pct in H1 1997.</title>
<headline>German natural gas imports dip 3.7 pct in H1 1997.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>German natural gas imports fell by 3.7 percent to 1.456 million terajoules in the first half of the year, the German economics agency (BAW) said on Monday.</p>
<p>However, the bill for the gas, imported from fields in Russia, the Netherlands, Norway, Denmark and the United Kingdom, rose by 24 percent to 6.4 billion marks. The price per unit of gas increased by an average 29 percent. -- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
